From a5384f69f77e5eb5c58d763c5fa5c05b4d941a50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:22:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 304/305] browser.c -- the RADIO tab can reload the station
 list

RLOD, in the footer slot UP was occupying and doing nothing in. That slot
was drawn disabled on the radio tab and refused in browser_touch(),
because UP is a volume operation and RADIO has no parent -- a dead button
in the corner the eye reaches first. Reload is the operation that tab
wants and had nowhere to be. It is enabled even with no stations at all,
which is the case it is most for: the status line already says "no
stations.m3u on the card", and the reason to read that is to go and make
one.

This is the open item from the 0200 series, and it is worth stating why
it stayed open. stations_load() opens a file and stations.h says in terms
not to call it from ui_task; a chooser that blocks on the card behind
live audio is the contention the storage arbiter exists to prevent. So
the button cannot do the thing it names.

It is therefore a request, answered across two tasks in the same split
s_open_chooser uses with the tasks swapped: ui_task returns
BROWSER_RELOAD_STATIONS and sets s_reload_stations, the player task does
the load in service_station_reload(), and ui_task rebuilds the rows.

Two details that are decisions rather than plumbing:

An epoch, not a flag, for the answer coming back. ui_task needs to know
the load HAS HAPPENED, and a request flag going false says only that
someone took it. Counting gives one rebuild per load and cannot be missed
by a pass that ran at the wrong moment.

Two call sites for the service, which is one more than is tidy. The idle
branch alone would have made RLOD work only when nothing was playing --
a button dead for the reason a user is least likely to guess -- and the
chooser opens over live audio, so a reload can be asked for there. Safe
from the decode loop because stations_load() reads at
STORAGE_IO_BACKGROUND, taking its own lease per chunk, so the PLAYBACK
lease wins every contest. That class exists for this and this is its
second user.

browser_stations_reloaded() guards on s_radio as well as s_open: it
arrives asynchronously from a load another task performed, and by then
the selected tab may be a directory listing, whose rows must not be
replaced by stations.

Also unblocks the 0300 series, which has now built and booted twice
without being exercised at all: every run has had no stations.m3u, so
nothing has drawn a LIVE badge, a station name or a lit next icon. A card
can be written and read without a reboot now.

Not flashed. browser.c produces no warnings the pre-patch file did not,
compiled against the texttest fakes at -O2.
