+
+The series entry says the thing the three patches have in common, since
+it is not what the 0200 series' lesson would have predicted: none of them
+was found by a board log. All three are a value that is correct and
+published and read by the wrong thing or by nothing, and each needed a
+second thing to have happened first -- a file played before a station, a
+list with two entries in it, a reader four thousand lines from its
+writer. That is the class of fault flashing early does not reach, and it
+is worth having beside the 0200 entry that argues for flashing early,
